@defgroup micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-deprecated-logical-functions Logical Functions
@brief Deprecated v5.0.1 names of the logical functions.

@details
The functions `mt::_and()`, `mt::_or()`, and `mt::_not()` are the v5.0.1
names of `mt::all_of()`, `mt::any_of()`, and `mt::negate()`. They are
deprecated since 5.1.0, and are kept for compatibility with the existing
applications; they behave as the functions that replace them.

The names were changed since a leading underscore is not used by the other
public names. Unlike the replacements, `mt::_and()` and `mt::_or()` take
exactly two operands, whereas `mt::all_of()` and `mt::any_of()` take two or
more.

| Deprecated    | Replacement    |
| ------------- | -------------- |
| `mt::_and()`  | `mt::all_of()` |
| `mt::_or()`   | `mt::any_of()` |
| `mt::_not()`  | `mt::negate()` |

@par Example

@code{.cpp}
// Deprecated.
t.expect (mt::_and (mt::eq (compute_answer (), 42),
                    mt::lt (compute_answer (), 43)));

// Replacement.
t.expect (mt::all_of (mt::eq (compute_answer (), 42),
                      mt::lt (compute_answer (), 43)));
@endcode

The overloaded logical operators of the `micro_test_plus::operators`
namespace are also deprecated since 5.1.0, in favour of the same
replacement functions.
